Article 12 The holder of the residence permit shall enjoy, in accordance with law, the right to employment, participation in social insurance, and contribution to, withdrawal and use of the housing provident fund in the place of residence. The people's government at or above the county level and its relevant departments shall provide the following basic public services for the holder of the residence permit:
(1) Compulsory education;
(2) Basic public employment services;
(3) Basic public health services and family planning services;
(4) Public cultural and sports services;
(5) Legal aid and other legal services;
(6) Other basic public services prescribed by the State.

Article 13 The holder of the residence permit shall enjoy the following conveniences in the place of residence:
(1) Applying for entry and exit documents in accordance with the relevant regulations of the State;
(2) Replacing or reissuing the resident identity card in accordance with the relevant regulations of the State;
(3) Registration of motor vehicles;
(4) Applying for a motor vehicle driver's license;
(5) Registering for professional qualification examinations and applying for the grant of professional qualifications;
(6) Applying for birth service registration and other family planning certification materials;
(7) Other conveniences prescribed by the State.

Article 18 Whoever commits any of the following acts shall be given a warning by the public security organ, ordered to make corrections, and fined not more than 200 yuan; if there are any illegal gains, the illegal gains shall be confiscated:
(1) Obtaining a residence permit by deception using false certification materials;
(2) Renting, lending or transferring the residence permit;
(3) Illegally detaining the residence permit of another person.

Article 20 Where any State organ or its staff member commits any of the following acts, the person shall be given a sanction according to law; if the act constitutes a crime, criminal liability shall be investigated according to law:
(1) Refusing to accept or issue a residence permit although the application meets the conditions for applying for a residence permit;
(2) Collecting fees in violation of the relevant provisions;
(3) Taking advantage of the convenience of producing or issuing residence permits to accept money or property from others or to seek other interests;
(4) Selling or illegally providing to others the personal information of the holders of the residence permit that they have learned in the course of work;
(5) Altering the information on the residence permit.
